WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.337
Use a repeatable checklist instead of choosing models by trial and error.

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:06.847
First define the task precisely.

00:00:06.847 --> 00:00:13.427
“Use AI on text” is too vague; “classify support tickets into five urgency levels” is actionable.

00:00:13.427 --> 00:00:18.142
Second choose the architecture or specialized model family that fits the output.

00:00:18.142 --> 00:00:20.592
Third verify language and domain.

00:00:20.592 --> 00:00:25.212
Fourth check model size, speed, memory, and deployment environment.

00:00:25.212 --> 00:00:29.537
Fifth read the model card, license, and evaluation results.

00:00:29.537 --> 00:00:34.297
Sixth test on your own examples, including difficult and edge cases.

00:00:34.297 --> 00:00:37.972
If the task is retrieval, measure retrieval quality.

00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:43.362
If it is classification, examine confusion matrices and per-class performance.

00:00:43.362 --> 00:00:49.107
If it is generation, check factuality and failure cases, not only fluency.

00:00:49.107 --> 00:00:53.712
The checklist is deliberately simple because model catalogs change.

00:00:53.712 --> 00:00:59.509
A stable decision process is more valuable than memorizing a list of currently popular checkpoints.
